    "id": "prop:commuting-sanity-reduction",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "If all fields \\(H_p(u)\\) are simultaneously diagonal in one fixed orthonormal basis for every \\(p\\in\\mathcal A\\) and \\(u\\in\\Omega\\), then every \\(C_{q\\leftarrow p}\\) is cyclically monotone and \\(\\gamma_{pq}=\\inf_{u\\in\\Omega}\\lambda_{\\min}(H_q(u)H_p(u)^{-1})>0\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "H_p",
      "p",
      "\\mathcal A",
      "u",
      "\\Omega",
      "C_{q\\leftarrow p}",
      "q",
      "\\gamma_{pq}",
      "H_q"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "thm:euclidean-frontier",
      "thm:cyclic-frontier",
      "ass:hessian-ellipticity",
      "def:cross-hessian-margin"
    ],
    "justification": "The reduction recovers ordinary scalar quantile rank preservation and a transparent multivariate commuting subclass.",
    "gap": "CarlierChernozhukovGalichon2016VQR recovers scalar conditional quantiles, but the commuting reduction checks that the new cross-Hessian notation collapses to that known benchmark.",
    "consumer": "Researchers can verify that the frontier does not alter classical scalar changes-in-changes or separable vector-quantile mechanisms.",
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(p,q\\in\\mathcal A\\).  In the common fixed orthonormal basis from the hypothesis, write\n\\[\n H_p(u)=\\operatorname{diag}(h_{p1}(u),\\ldots,h_{pd}(u)),\n \\qquad\n H_q(u)=\\operatorname{diag}(h_{q1}(u),\\ldots,h_{qd}(u)).\n\\]\nBy \\(\\mathrm{ass:hessian\\text{-}ellipticity}\\),\n\\[\n m\\le h_{pj}(u),h_{qj}(u)\\le M\n \\qquad(1\\le j\\le d).\n\\]\nThe two Hessians commute pointwise, so \\(\\mathrm{thm:cyclic\\text{-}frontier}\\) makes \\(C_{q\\leftarrow p}\\) cyclically monotone.  Moreover,\n\\[\n H_q(u)H_p(u)^{-1}\n =\\operatorname{diag}\\!\\left(\\frac{h_{q1}(u)}{h_{p1}(u)},\\ldots,\n \\frac{h_{qd}(u)}{h_{pd}(u)}\\right)\n \\succeq\\frac mM I_d.\n\\]\nIt is already symmetric, and \\(\\mathrm{def:cross\\text{-}hessian\\text{-}margin}\\) therefore gives\n\\[\n \\gamma_{pq}\n =\\inf_{u\\in\\Omega}\\min_j\\frac{h_{qj}(u)}{h_{pj}(u)}\n \\ge\\frac mM>0.\n\\]\nThis also agrees with the strong Euclidean monotonicity conclusion of \\(\\mathrm{thm:euclidean\\text{-}frontier}\\).",
